#X text 3568 -530 DEBUG TAPS (added to trace the load/play flow) -- GOTPATH = the raw "sourceSlot path" list this instance received from buffer_manager_bridge.js's resolvePath reply (route's gotPath outlet \, obj 1). SRC0-READMSG / SRC1-READMSG = the fully-built "read -resize <path> src_N_<stem>-0 src_N_<stem>-1" message (obj 62 / 66) -- this is what WOULD go to a [soundfiler] if one existed downstream of this abstraction's outlet \; as of 2026-08-19 there is no [soundfiler] object anywhere in this file or in gnumbat-analyze.pd's wiring of it \, so trace where this message's outlet (obj 4 for src_0 \, obj 4 for src_1 too -- both land on the SAME outlet\\\, outlet index 1 of this abstraction) goes in the parent patch to find out whether anything downstream actually reads the file. RING0-SIZE / RING1-SIZE = [array size ring_N_<stem>-0] (obj 293 / 300) \, queried on ring-related dispatch -- shows the frame count Pd currently has for the ring buffer that the slicer engine's segment composition writes into., f 70;
#X obj -545 542 pack f f f;
#X obj -595 595 list prepend prepare;
#X msg -595 645 commit;
#X text 3567 -285 PLAY->PREPARE/COMMIT WIRE (added 2026-08-21) -- Bug 3 fix: "play" (obj 1 outlet0 -> unpack obj 67) previously had NO path to ever emit prepare/commit toward slot_router\\\; only the deferred ring-buffer "ringDone" path (obj 391-398) could. This taps obj 67's outlet0 (slot\\\, fires LAST in unpack's right-to-left cascade) as the pack's hot inlet\\\, and outlets 4/3 (segDurMs/stretchR) as its cold inlets\\\, so both cold values are set before the hot inlet fires. Reuses the same terminal outlet (obj 7 = outlet index 4) that the ring-buffer path already uses\\\, so buffer_manager.pd/slot_router.pd need no changes for this to reach them.;
