#X text 3568 -100 SRC BUFFER LOAD + DURATION REPORT (added 2026-08-21) -- the "read -resize <path> src_N_\$1-0 src_N_\$1-1" messages built above (obj 62 / 66) were built but never sent anywhere that actually reads the file -- confirmed via BUFMGR-SRC0/1-READMSG taps and array size always reading 0/stale. 410 is the actual [soundfiler] that was missing\\\; its outlet (frames read) also bangs 166 directly (self-triggered "srcDone" \, parallel to the existing external-inlet path) and feeds 411's "t b f" \, which computes ms from the real live samplerate (412/413 \, same pattern gnumbat-analyze.pd's own need_stemDurs chain uses) \, looks up this instance's full track name from its short-code creation arg (416/417/418-421 \, since setStemDurMs's OSC target expects "vocals" not "voc") \, and sends "setStemDurMs <track> <ms>" out via the SAME outlet (obj 4 / outlet index 1) the dead read-message already used -- see gnumbat-analyze.pd's new wiring of buffer_manager's per-stem outlets into bridge_slicer for the rest of the path. Fires once per src_0 read and once per src_1 read (same file \, same duration \, harmless double-report)., f 70;
#X obj -608 710 list trim;
