#X text 3571 152 LIST-TRIM FIX (added 2026-08-21) -- [list prepend prepare] (407) does not produce a genuine "prepare"-selector message on its own (confirmed live: buffer_manager_stem_unknown_msg printed "list play ..." for the equivalent play-tagging in buffer_manager.pd instead of matching route's "play" case) -- it stays selector "list" with "prepare" as just the first data atom. 425/426 strip that wrapper (same [list trim] already used for the read-message builders above) before 407/408's output reaches outlet 7 and buffer_manager.pd's per-stem "route prepare commit stop resume".;
#X obj 2803 1296 list trim;
#X obj 763 2461 list trim;
#X obj 1099 1397 list trim;
#X text 3571 302 ARRAY-DECLARATION FIX (added 2026-08-21) -- the "read -resize <path> src_N_\$1-0 src_N_\$1-1" messages (obj 62/66) and 410's [soundfiler] were built earlier this session\\\, but soundfiler's -resize flag can only resize an array that ALREADY EXISTS as a declared Pd array -- it cannot create one from nothing. These 4 arrays were never declared anywhere (unlike the pre-existing \$0-srcSlotContents array just above)\\\, so every read failed with "array: couldn't find named array 'src_0_<code>-0'" etc. and the duration report never fired with real data. These 4 declarations (mirroring \$0-srcSlotContents's own subpatch-array pattern) give soundfiler real arrays to resize into -- \$1 substitutes to this instance's short code (voc/drm/bss/mel) same as everywhere else in this file\\\, so each of the 4 instances gets its own uniquely-named set. Declared size 2 is just a placeholder -- -resize overwrites it with the real frame count on every read., f 70;
#X text 3573 516 RING/BAKE BUFCOMPOSE LIST-TRIM FIX (added 2026-08-21) -- found live via a user-added print tap on buffer_manager's outlet toward bass's fluid.bufcompose: "list source src_0_bss" / "list destination ring_1_bss" instead of genuine "source"/"destination" selector messages -- fluid.bufcompose replied "no method for 'symbol'" for both\\\, i.e. it never actually composed anything into the ring buffer. Root cause is the SAME [list prepend X] wrapper bug fixed everywhere else this session: 349-371 (12x list prepend source/destination\\\, feeding outlet index 2 / obj 5 -- the ring-buffer prep/compose path) and 373-387 (8x\\\, feeding outlet index 3 / obj 6 -- the bake snapshot/restore compose path) all built "list source ..."/"list destination ..." instead of a real selector. 429/430 are shared [list trim]s (one per outlet -- all 12/8 sources fan into the same trim since Pd processes them one at a time\\\, not concurrently) stripping the wrapper before either group reaches fluid.bufcompose. The other messages on these same chains ("startframe \$1"\\\, "numframes \$1"\\\, "deststartframe 0"\\\, "bang") were already fine -- they're literal msg-box text\\\, not built via list prepend -- matching exactly what the live BUFCOMPOSEBASS print showed (everything correct except source/destination)., f 70;
#X obj 648 484 list prepend set;
#X obj 648 525 list trim;
#X text 3577 823 RING-SLOT PLAYBACK SWITCH (added 2026-08-21) -- porting the original Max buffer_manager.js design\\\, where every ring-compose also sent karma~ a "set ring_<slot>_<stem>" so playback actually used the freshly-written buffer (see buffer_manager.js's own top-of-file comment: "After compose: ring.active <-> ring.staging swap\\\; karma~ plays ring.active."). Until now this Pd port only wrote INTO ring_0/1_\$1 (the bufcompose fix above) -- nothing ever told stem_timestretch~ to switch to reading FROM it\\\, so it kept playing the full \$1-mono buffer forever regardless of any composed segment. 350/352/356/358 (the SAME \$0-ringActive-gated symbol resolution already used to pick fluid.bufcompose's destination) now ALSO write their resolved name into 437 (write instance) in parallel with the existing "list prepend destination" feed -- construction only\\\, doesn't send anything yet. The actual send is gated on the compose bang itself (124 for the src_0 cluster\\\, 158 for src_1) via a NEW connection added AFTER each bang's existing "-> 5 0" line (Pd fires same-outlet connections in file order -- confirmed by checking 67's own two "outlet 0" connections\\\, which is how this file's existing play-vs-ring-compose ordering already works)\\\, so "set" only reaches 7 (outlet index 4\\\, same outlet prepare/commit/stop/resume already use) once fluid.bufcompose has actually finished writing. 438 is a second read-only \$0-ringSetName instance (same underlying storage\\\, separate object purely for wiring clarity) banged by both compose triggers -> 439 rebuilds a genuine "set" selector (list prepend doesn't produce one on its own\\\, same bug fixed everywhere else this session) -> 440 trims the "list" wrapper before it reaches 7 ASSUMPTION NOT YET VERIFIED BY A LIVE TEST: this relies on fluid.bufcompose completing its copy synchronously within the same logical-time message cascade\\\, with no async/deferred completion -- if it turns out fluid.bufcompose defers\\\, "set" could fire before the write actually lands and this needs a real completion signal instead of assuming same-tick ordering. NOT PORTED: the original's cross-stem sync barrier (cycleTracker in buffer_manager.js) that held every stem's commit until its whole sync group was ready -- this port commits each stem the moment ITS OWN compose finishes\\\, same "known simplification" already documented in slot_router_stem.pd for commit/resume-before-prep., f 80;
#X text 3578 1300 RING-SET RACE FIX (2026-08-25) -- traced live: the "set <ringname>" relay added 2026-08-21 (438-440 -> outlet 7) was triggered from 124/158\\\, the SAME bang that kicks off the ring-compose request (fed from 105/139\\\, part of the pending-segment SETUP cascade -- confirmed by tracing 105 other outlets into \$0-pendSeg/pendStretch/pendCyc/pendGrp)\\\, not from the actual completion. The real completion signal is "ringDone"\\\, which arrives later as a SEPARATE message via the parent canvas fluid.bufcompose object (its outlet 0 bangs once it finishes writing -> "ring_done <stem>" -> buffer_manager -> back down into this instance route\\\, outlet 3) and lands on 260\\\, a completely different subtree (cpHas/spigot/next-prepare/"ready") that never touched 438 So "set" was reaching stem_timestretch~ at the moment a compose was REQUESTED\\\, not after it landed -- on a stem first play this points \$0-curArray at a ring array that has never been written (0 frames)\\\, so timeStretch~ computes durMs=0 and nothing audible plays\\\, which is exactly the "ASSUMPTION NOT YET VERIFIED" flagged in the 2026-08-21 comment above. Fix: removed 124->438 and 158->438\\\, added 260->438 instead\\\, so the stored \$0-ringSetName (already written at prepare-time by 350/352/356/358) is only read and relayed as "set" once the real ringDone completion for this instance has actually arrived. No other wiring changed., f 70;
